Invoice number must not be empty.
Vendor name must not be empty.
Invoice date must be valid.
Due date must be valid where required.
Invoice amount must be numeric.
Quantity must be valid where applicable.
Unit price must be valid where applicable.
Currency must be recognised.
Tax calculations must be verified.
Subtotal must match line-item calculations.
Total amount must match the documented formula.
Negative amounts must be flagged for review.
Missing mandatory fields must be identified.
Invalid date formats must be detected.
Invalid numeric values must be detected.
Make validation rules configurable.
Do not assume that all countries use the
same tax rules or date formats.
Use configurable financial rounding tolerances.
For example:
Expected Total =
Subtotal + Tax + Shipping - Discount
