ADDITIONAL LOG FILE REQUIREMENT
==================================================
Implement a real and functional application logging
system that records important application activities
and events in actual log files.

LOG FILE PURPOSE:
Maintain a permanent, traceable record of application
activities, processing operations, errors, and system
events for debugging, monitoring, and auditing.

LOG FILE ACTIVITIES:
Record the following events:
Application Started.
Application Stopped.
User Login and Logout, if authentication exists.
File Uploaded.
File Upload Failed.
File Validation Started.
File Validation Completed.
Invoice Processing Started.
Invoice Processing Completed.
Number of Records Detected.
Number of Valid Invoices.
Number of Invalid Invoices.
Number of Duplicate Invoices.
Exception Detection.
Exception Resolution.
Reconciliation Started.
Reconciliation Completed.
Report Generation Started.
Report Generation Completed.
Report Downloaded.
Settings Updated.
Unexpected Errors.
System Warnings.

LOG FILE FORMAT:
Create actual log files in a dedicated logs directory.

Example:
logs/
    application.log
    error.log
    processing.log
    audit.log

Each log entry must include:
Timestamp.
Log Level.
Module Name.
Action or Event.
Relevant Record or File Reference, where applicable.
Detailed Message.
Processing Status.

LOG LEVELS:
INFO.
WARNING.
ERROR.
CRITICAL.
DEBUG.

LOG FILE EXAMPLE:
2026-11-09 10:00:00 | INFO | SYSTEM |
Application Started | SUCCESS

2026-11-09 10:05:00 | INFO | UPLOAD |
Invoice.xlsx Uploaded | SUCCESS

2026-11-09 10:06:00 | INFO | PROCESSING |
100 Invoice Records Detected | SUCCESS

2026-11-09 10:07:00 | INFO | VALIDATION |
85 Valid Invoices Identified | SUCCESS

2026-11-09 10:07:30 | WARNING | VALIDATION |
10 Invalid Invoices Identified | REVIEW REQUIRED

2026-11-09 10:08:00 | WARNING | DUPLICATE |
5 Duplicate Invoices Identified | REVIEW REQUIRED

2026-11-09 10:09:00 | INFO | REPORT |
Excel Report Generated | SUCCESS

FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS:
Use Python logging or an equivalent reliable
logging framework.
Create log files automatically when the application
starts.
Use appropriate log levels.
Implement exception logging with useful error details.
Record processing start and completion timestamps.
Record failed operations and their causes.
Support log file rotation to prevent unlimited
log file growth.
Keep logs organised by date or category where useful.
Provide a Log Viewer page or section in the application.
Allow authorised users to:
View recent log entries.
Search logs.
Filter by date.
Filter by log level.
Filter by module.
View error details.
Download log files.
Export selected logs when appropriate.

SECURITY REQUIREMENTS:
Do not record passwords.
Do not record API keys or authentication tokens.
Do not expose confidential invoice information
unnecessarily in log messages.
Sanitise sensitive data before writing logs.
Restrict access to log files according to
appropriate user permissions.
Protect logs from unauthorised modification
where technically feasible.

IMPORTANT:
Logs must be generated from actual application events.
Do not display fabricated log entries.
Do not create a UI-only Log Viewer.
The logging system must be connected to the real
backend processing, validation, upload, reporting,
and exception-management operations.
If an operation fails, record the actual failure.
Do not claim that an operation succeeded unless
it actually completed successfully.
